      {
        "text": "# Human-Centered Reliability\n\n**Human-centered reliability** is the design practice of making sure an application is helpful and transparent to the user even when technical errors occur. \n\n>Imagine you are on a flight and the plane hits unexpected turbulence.\n>\n>**Low Reliability:** The pilot says nothing and you wonder if you are in danger. \n>\n>**Human-Centered Reliability:** The pilot immediately speaks over the intercom and says, \"We're hitting some choppy air, but the plane is built for this. We’ll be through it in five minutes.\"\n",
        "imageUrl": "https://images.code.org/0b6a2f7ca73a798e513a8b882c5f7969-Screenshot 2026-02-17 at 3.44.53 PM.png",
